WEBVTT

00:00:05.519 --> 00:00:10.070
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twenty-fifth. Can you all hear me over that fan?</v>

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:19.309
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, just. My grand weekend plans ended up being sitting indoors watching the rain. Weather forecast absolutely stitched us up.</v>

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.420
<v Marcus Hale>Bank holiday weather, that. Comes as part of the package.</v>

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:30.370
<v Aisha Begum>On a brighter note, there's a birthday cake in the office. Under the blue lid.</v>

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:35.590
<v Jamie Brennan>Ah. That explains the very clean knife and the suspiciously large missing bit.</v>

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:40.340
<v Aisha Begum>Not naming names. Mostly because I've still got crumbs on me.</v>

00:00:41.969 --> 00:00:45.469
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a cake investigation. What's already finished?</v>

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:54.570
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah so, I tested the Gas Turbine 1 yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished, nothing outstanding from that test.</v>

00:00:55.770 --> 00:01:00.320
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, it's been behaving since. Much nicer shift without that hanging over us.</v>

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:06.230
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. Just closing the loop, not putting it back on today's list.</v>

00:01:07.659 --> 00:01:14.310
<v Fiona Doyle>And I already swapped the filter on the pick and place on two yesterday. That one's done as well.</v>

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:22.379
<v David Whitfield>I saw the pressure on the pick and place on two dip for a few minutes. Came back on its own, though.</v>

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.200
<v Hannah Price>Was that a continuing drop, or just that little patch?</v>

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:35.980
<v David Whitfield>Just that patch. No ongoing fault to report; it recovered without anyone touching it. Only an observation.</v>

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.530
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, noted as an observation, not another job.</v>

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:47.069
<v Fiona Doyle>The supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the Main Outfeed Conveyor, either. Same blocker as before.</v>

00:01:48.969 --> 00:01:53.519
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, there's no confirmed delivery showing on my side. Nothing new behind that.</v>

00:01:55.269 --> 00:01:59.469
<v Sarah Okafor>That stays blocked, then. No fresh action out of that this morning.</v>

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:06.739
<v Sarah Okafor>Dave, can you clear the jam and check the sensors on the Palletiser, Monday? That's today.</v>

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:13.620
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, um—is that the jam itself and the sensor checks, rather than just getting it moving again?</v>

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:20.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Both, please. Clear the jam and check the sensors on the Palletiser.</v>

00:02:22.189 --> 00:02:25.340
<v David Whitfield>Right, I'll do both on the Palletiser today, Monday.</v>

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:31.659
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, your last bit went all robotic there. I heard 'both', then a sort of underwater noise.</v>

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:37.120
<v David Whitfield>That might just be my normal voice. But yes, both, today.</v>

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:44.180
<v Sarah Okafor>And Dave, can you take vibration readings on the compressor one, Monday as well? No rush on that.</v>

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:49.680
<v David Whitfield>Readings only for that one, yeah? Not rolling the bearing greasing into it?</v>

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:56.020
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right. This one's just the vibration readings on the compressor one. Separate from the bearing work.</v>

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:02.360
<v David Whitfield>Yep, I'll take the vibration readings on the compressor one Monday. Understood, no rush.</v>

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:11.310
<v Marcus Hale>On that separate bit, we do need someone to grease and check the bearings on the compressor one tomorrow. No rush, though.</v>

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.159
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone able to take that bearing job?</v>

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:24.699
<v David Whitfield>I can't commit to that as well. Don't put it against me just because I'm doing the readings.</v>

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:29.490
<v Marcus Hale>No, and I'm only flagging it, not volunteering for it.</v>

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:37.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, nobody on it. Grease and check the bearings on the compressor one remains unallocated, due tomorrow, no rush.</v>

00:03:38.719 --> 00:03:43.969
<v Fiona Doyle>Um, I'll send the shift handover report round by Thursday. It's fairly important, that one.</v>

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:49.169
<v Hannah Price>That's the shift handover report we've been talking about, not a separate quality report?</v>

00:03:50.979 --> 00:03:55.180
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, that same shift handover report. I'll get it round by Thursday.</v>

00:03:56.719 --> 00:03:58.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fiona. Got that.</v>

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:04.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you schedule downtime for the dryer with production, tomorrow?</v>

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:15.879
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah—just so we're saying the same thing, tomorrow is when I need to get the downtime scheduled, not a promise that the dryer will actually be down tomorrow?</v>

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:23.600
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Schedule it with production tomorrow. We're not setting the shutdown date in this call.</v>

00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:27.889
<v Jamie Brennan>Fine, I'll schedule downtime for the dryer with production tomorrow.</v>

00:04:28.569 --> 00:04:35.220
<v Fiona Doyle>Glad you separated those. 'Scheduled tomorrow' and 'scheduled for tomorrow' get treated as the same thing far too often.</v>

00:04:35.569 --> 00:04:39.769
<v Jamie Brennan>Usually about thirty seconds before someone asks where all their output's gone.</v>

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:46.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona, can you recalibrate the sensors on the line 3 chiller Monday? Fairly important.</v>

00:04:48.079 --> 00:04:53.329
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the line 3 chiller Monday. Got it, fairly important.</v>

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:58.240
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, Monday as in today? Teams clipped the start for me.</v>

00:04:59.779 --> 00:05:01.529
<v Sarah Okafor>Today, yes. Monday the twenty-fifth.</v>

00:05:02.189 --> 00:05:06.040
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, that's what I've got for the line 3 chiller. Today.</v>

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:17.879
<v David Whitfield>And I'll book a contractor to look at the stretch wrapper. That's a whenever you get a chance one, isn't it? I'll take it on that basis.</v>

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:27.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, Davey, whenever you get a chance. Booking a contractor to look at the stretch wrapper, not promising a visit date here.</v>

00:05:29.699 --> 00:05:34.250
<v David Whitfield>Exactly. I'll make the booking; no fixed date being agreed on this call.</v>

00:05:35.769 --> 00:05:38.220
<v Marcus Hale>Different name for the contractor jobs, then?</v>

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:42.129
<v David Whitfield>Same bloke, unfortunately. No extra pair of hands included.</v>

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:51.569
<v Sarah Okafor>And to avoid any crossed wires, the bearings on the compressor one still have nobody. The readings being covered doesn't change that.</v>

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:58.620
<v Fiona Doyle>Likewise, that Main Outfeed Conveyor delivery is still unconfirmed. Wouldn't want the blocker to sound like a delivery promise.</v>

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.420
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed. Still blocked, nothing newly assigned there.</v>

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:08.829
<v Hannah Price>All clear from me. Nothing else to add to the list.</v>

00:06:09.639 --> 00:06:14.889
<v Aisha Begum>Same here. And the cake was information, by the way, not a compulsory team activity.</v>

00:06:16.639 --> 00:06:19.790
<v Jamie Brennan>Good. I'd hate to have to record my slice.</v>

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:23.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's us. Thanks, everyone.</v>
